      "content": "idk, i dont see how small actions change the outcome of a global catastrophe. everything feels so terminal. sometimes i look at the future and i just dont see myself in it. it seems easier to just not have to witness the collapse if i wasn't here to see it happen. does that make sense? like, why endure the slow decay?",
